      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you are experiencing a genuine existential crisis where your life's structure suddenly collapsed. When the purpose vanishes, the immediate task isn't finding a new \"big\" purpose, but simply surviving the day. Focus only on the smallest routines—a shower, a cup of tea, going outside for five minutes—as these tiny acts become your new, necessary anchors. These small gestures are not \"navigating\" the void, but rather keeping the fragile engine idling until you feel ready to try turning it over.",
